# Patch: agent alternate config open + section nav/fold + cursor persist
# Plugin: ravitemer/mcphub.nvim
# Tested against: 163b3ad [v6.2.0] with local patches 01-14 applied
#
# 1. config_alternates on CLI agent rows: each target provides key/label/path/matcher.
#    Non-conflicting keys register as main-view keymaps; pressing the key on an
#    agent_binding row opens the target file and jumps to the matcher location.
#    Matcher uses dot-path navigation for JSON/TOML/YAML (plain-text fallback).
#    JSON terminal-key search prefers the shallowest (root-level) match so
#    `.mcpServers` lands on the root key, not a nested duplicate inside `projects`.
#
# 2. Cursor persists across UI toggle: cleanup() calls before_leave() so position
#    is saved and restored when the UI is reopened with :MCPHub.
#
# 3. Section navigation and fold in main browse mode:
#    J / K  — jump to next / previous section header (wraps); shown in footer
#    h / l  — on a foldable section header: fold / unfold (▶/▼ prefix icon)
#              on any other line: original server collapse/expand behavior
#    Foldable sections (▼/▶ prefix): Global group, Project group,
#                       Native Servers, Endpoints, CLI Agents, Active Hubs
#    MCP Servers header is a nav anchor only (not foldable, no triangle).
#
# 4. Token display: "~1.2kt" / "~123t" → "~1.2k" / "~123" (drop trailing 't').
#    Also simplifies the MCP Servers total: "(~1.2k)" instead of "(~ 1.2k tokens)".
#
# Consumer config_alternates example:
#   config_alternates = {
#     { key = "1", path = "~/.claude/settings.json", matcher = ".permissions" },
#     { key = "2", path = "~/.claude.json",          matcher = ".mcpServers"  },
#   }
#
# Paths can use `~` or `$HOME`; they are expanded before opening.
# Server build dependency: none. Client/UI behavior only.
